      "writtenOn": "2020-08-03T14:44:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For safety, should we always reserve the legacy P2P prefix, even if the setting is off?\n\nWhat if:\n\n1. The config option is disabled, and shouldEnableWifiP2pDedicatedIp() returns false.\n2. USB or wifi tethering is enabled and we pick 192.168.49.xxx.\n3. The configuration changes (e.g., due to MCC/MNC change, RRO app update, ...) and shouldEnableWifiP2pDedicatedIp starts returning true.\n4. The user enables wifi p2p.",
      "range": {
